.TH CRYPTO\-INVENTORY 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded 6b26b19a" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
crypto\-inventory \- Build and check the Kingdom's cryptographic bill of materials (CBOM).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crypto\-inventory
COMMAND [OPTION]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Build and check the Kingdom's cryptographic bill of materials (CBOM).
Paths given to \-\-out, \-\-cbom and \-\-baseline are relative to the repository root (or absolute inside it); the tool reads and writes nothing outside it.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
regenerate the CBOM (\-\-out PATH, default stdout)
.TP
.B check
exit 1 when the checked\-in CBOM differs from a regeneration
.TP
.B summary
count components by pq\-status
.TP
.B collect\-host
write one host's read\-only crypto facts (\-\-host, \-\-local | \-\-ssh, \-\-out)
.TP
.B lint
exit 1 on classical\-only key exchange not in the shrink\-only baseline (\-\-baseline FILE, \-\-update refuses additions, \-\-print, \-\-explain PATH)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 finding, 2 usage or error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
